  partName: Intake Runner (2)
  description: The Intake Runner (2) is a medium-sized, elongated metal component
    located at the middle-center-front of the engine, responsible for directing air
    into the combustion chamber. Its bright metal finish indicates a high-temperature
    resistant material, which is crucial for withstanding the intense heat generated
    during the combustion process. Interestingly, the intake runner's shape is optimized
    to minimize airflow restrictions and maximize engine performance.
